Falsifies `non_volatile_memory_express::verification::cq_pop_stays_in_bounds_and_flips_only_at_the_wrap`.

The defect: `CompletionQueue::pop` wraps one slot early (`>= entries - 1`), so the last completion slot is
never read and the phase flips a slot too soon. **This patch does not turn the original harness
red**: the head stays in bounds, the returned value equals the head and the phase flips exactly
when the head reads zero, all of which an early wrap satisfies. The record is for the harness as
strengthened in the same change, which also asserts the head advanced by exactly one modulo the
ring.

Expected to fail: the added `assert_eq!(cq.head, (head + 1) % entries)`: a pop from `entries - 2` lands on slot 0
instead of `entries - 1`.

